+\pipelinecaption{fig:blame-conflict}{Different inputs, identical recovery outputs.
+The minimum BLAME term selects the successor; independently, the highest
+admissible QC selects the anchor. ``Minimum'' refers to the common agreed
+reports, not the first certificate received or every certificate ever formed.
+Choosing Bob does not make him honest: $(e+1,1)$ is a fresh voting identity.
+Old $\BC_{(e,1)}$ cannot abort it; a fresh failure can lead to the next recovery.}
